{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"SessionStart","additionalContext":"This run is governed by Tego, which enforces the run's contract in the kernel. When Tego refuses an action, the system call fails with EACCES or EPERM (a refused command commonly exits with status 126), and the reason is written to \"$REASON\": a JSON file (v 1) whose top level is the latest refusal, with refusals counting every refusal of the run and recent listing up to the newest 32, each with its seq, reason, rule and a one-sentence text. The run's contract decides what is allowed, and the run cannot change it. Each refusal is also reported once, in a note beside the tool result that follows it or at the end of the turn."}}
